  {
    "sha": "7c46c4d4cf2356b15bad34f9f9bdebf93274090d",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDdjNDZjNGQ0Y2YyMzU2YjE1YmFkMzRmOWY5YmRlYmY5MzI3NDA5MGQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-17T16:33:34Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-17T16:33:34Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(test): pin the #2004 depth ladder in two heavy motion lanes\n\nPR #2013 (#2004) starts the depth ladder one stepdown under Top Z, so\nthe air level at Top Z is gone. It updated the debug twins but not two\nignored heavy-lane tests, which the v0.23.0 release preflight ran red.\n\n- adaptive_hsm a_small_helix_rectangle_never_crosses_itself: Top 0,\n  Bottom -4, Stepdown 2 now cuts [-2, -4]: two helices, not three. The\n  test now also pins that each helix lands on -2 and -4.\n- rotary_adaptive the_r62_neck_levels_are_hsm_planned_on_microlift_returns:\n  the r6.2 skin level (air over the r6 bar) is gone; assert that no\n  level is cut on the skin, as a_window_too_narrow_... does for r7. The\n  5.7 and 5.2 neck-level asserts are unchanged.\n\nRefs #2369\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
