  {
    "sha": "207596999b189c85cfbe34c240bb824572cf2316",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDIwNzU5Njk5OWIxODljODVjZmJlMzRjMjQwYmI4MjQ1NzJjZjIzMTY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-17T18:28:21Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-17T18:28:21Z"
      },
      "message": "test(app): re-measure the bore's HSM triple after the depth ladder change\n\nThe release gate of v0.23.0 (Linux cut runner, run 44127297984) failed\npocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean\nwith (4726, 4698, 549) against the pinned (16029, 15372, 1427).\n\nCause: #2004 (PR #2013) starts the depth ladder one stepdown under Top Z\nwhen no stock stands over Top Z. This job has Top Z = stock top = Z 20,\nso its level at Z 20 cut only air and is now gone.\n\nProof (Windows x86_64, release, per-level breakdown):\n- f887908f9 (first parent of the #2013 merge feabe2524): (16017, 15360,\n  1427), the old Windows pin. Z 20 segment: 11303 moves, 10672 planar\n  feeds, 878 arcs - feeds at Z 20 over the part's top face (X -25..25,\n  Y -25..14.7) and microlift returns at Z 20.3..21.2; nothing under the\n  stock top.\n- 7c46c4d4c: (4716, 4688, 549), two runs identical. Levels Z 15 / 10 /\n  5 / 0: 383/376/74, 3567/3560/327, 383/376/74, 377/376/74 (moves,\n  planar, arcs) - the same before and after.\n- From the first Z 15 feed on, the 4710 moves are identical at both\n  commits (same hash of their Debug form). Only the entry before Z 15\n  changed (4 -> 6 moves). Every level verifies clean.\n\nWindows arm (4716, 4688, 549); Linux arm (4726, 4698, 549) from the cut\nrunner. The macOS aarch64 pin is stale and not measurable here: macOS\ngoes to the band arm (both measured triples +-10) until issue #2371\nmeasures it.\n\nRefs #2369\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
